{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146460",
      "title": "Analyzing Further Authentication Requirements",
      "lectureOrder": 409,
      "videoOrder": 377,
      "sourceHash": "ad4e6406e098914fd48f9d0786b2091263748cffc7d07af48a07a3a50da507de",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.33,
          "end": 3.63,
          "en": "Over the last lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.63,
          "end": 5.29,
          "en": "we ensured that we can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.29,
          "end": 8.06,
          "en": "log in and log out and create users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.06,
          "end": 11.2,
          "en": "And that we protect certain pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.2,
          "end": 14.26,
          "en": "And that we control which page can be visited,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.26,
          "end": 16.84,
          "en": "if we're locked in or locked out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.84,
          "end": 19.01,
          "en": "That certain pages like the profile page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.01,
          "end": 22.5,
          "en": "can't be visited that were redirected automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.5,
          "end": 24.89,
          "en": "And all of that works now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.89,
          "end": 28.97,
          "en": "All of that works with help of the Next Auth package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.97,
          "end": 32.6,
          "en": "and the session which it checks for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.6,
          "end": 34.39,
          "en": "And just to make this really clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.39,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "when I say session here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 39.73,
          "en": "I am talking about this json web token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.73,
          "end": 43.11,
          "en": "Which is managed automatically by Next Auth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.11,
          "end": 45.04,
          "en": "Which is stored by Next Auth",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.04,
          "end": 48.55,
          "en": "in our browser this cookie,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.55,
          "end": 51.21,
          "en": "which holds this token is created there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.21,
          "end": 53.64,
          "en": "And Next Auth determines whether",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.64,
          "end": 55.61,
          "en": "we have an active session,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.61,
          "end": 57.9,
          "en": "so if this user is logged in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.9,
          "end": 60.5,
          "en": "by checking that cookie and that token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.5,
          "end": 62.44,
          "en": "that's stored in that cookie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.44,
          "end": 65.49,
          "en": "That is what happens when we call getsession here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.49,
          "end": 69.05,
          "en": "or in our main-navigation component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.05,
          "end": 71.56,
          "en": "when we use the useSession hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.56,
          "end": 74.093,
          "en": "And that's what we did up to this point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.95,
          "end": 77.72,
          "en": "Now one crucial feature is missing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.72,
          "end": 81.73,
          "en": "one of the main reasons for adding authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.73,
          "end": 86.01,
          "en": "Because having this client site protection here is nice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.01,
          "end": 88.65,
          "en": "protecting certain pages and making sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.65,
          "end": 90.82,
          "en": "we can't reach certain pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.82,
          "end": 92.99000000000001,
          "en": "is all nice and good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 92.99000000000001,
          "end": 94.41,
          "en": "But what really matters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.41,
          "end": 96.81,
          "en": "is what we as a user can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.81,
          "end": 99.52000000000001,
          "en": "Which API routes we can hit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.52000000000001,
          "end": 102.64,
          "en": "Here we got this change password example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.64,
          "end": 104.17,
          "en": "But of course for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.17,
          "end": 105.97,
          "en": "if you're building an online shop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 105.97,
          "end": 109.63,
          "en": "you might only want to allow logged in users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.63,
          "end": 113.31,
          "en": "to create and delete and manage products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.31,
          "end": 116.05,
          "en": "And in the interface which your website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.05,
          "end": 118.34,
          "en": "has for managing those products,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.34,
          "end": 121.625,
          "en": "you would be sending requests behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.625,
          "end": 124.56,
          "en": "to certain API end points,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 124.56,
          "end": 126.77,
          "en": "certain API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126.77,
          "end": 130.85,
          "en": "Where those requests then trigger certain operations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.85,
          "end": 132.63,
          "en": "Like the creation of a product",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 132.63,
          "end": 135.13,
          "en": "or the deletion of a product.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 135.13,
          "end": 137.87,
          "en": "And of course you want to make sure that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 137.87,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "those requests only trigger those operations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 144.5,
          "en": "if they come from authenticated users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 144.5,
          "end": 148.17000000000002,
          "en": "So that if you have API routes in your project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 151.2,
          "en": "API routes that do certain operations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 151.2,
          "end": 154.7,
          "en": "that are only allowed for authenticated users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 154.7,
          "end": 158.66,
          "en": "that in those API routes you also verify,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 158.66,
          "end": 160.63,
          "en": "whether that request is coming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 160.63,
          "end": 163.32999999999998,
          "en": "from an authenticated user or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 163.32999999999998,
          "end": 165.87,
          "en": "Because even if you have full control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 165.87,
          "end": 167.92000000000002,
          "en": "over this user interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 167.92000000000002,
          "end": 172.92000000000002,
          "en": "requests to APIs can also be sent with other tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 173.29,
          "end": 176.53,
          "en": "From the command line, with tools like Postman",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 176.53,
          "end": 179.57999999999998,
          "en": "which allows you to create http requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 179.57999999999998,
          "end": 183.65,
          "en": "So there are ways of sending requests to APIs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 183.65,
          "end": 186.7,
          "en": "that don't require your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 186.7,
          "end": 190.17,
          "en": "And therefore protecting the pages on those websites,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 190.17,
          "end": 193.2,
          "en": "is one thing but we also need protection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 193.2,
          "end": 195.32,
          "en": "in those API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 195.32,
          "end": 198.18,
          "en": "Where we validate incoming requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 198.18,
          "end": 201.1,
          "en": "and double check that this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 201.1,
          "end": 204.14,
          "en": "is coming from an authenticated source.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 204.14,
          "end": 205.82999999999998,
          "en": "And I'm emphasizing this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 205.82999999999998,
          "end": 209.89,
          "en": "because this is another key part of authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 209.89,
          "end": 212.3,
          "en": "It's not just about the client site,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 212.3,
          "end": 214.56,
          "en": "it is also about the server site ,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 214.56,
          "end": 216.95,
          "en": "about those API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 216.95,
          "end": 218.94,
          "en": "And that's therefore what we're going to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 218.94,
          "end": 220.833,
          "en": "take a closer look at now.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
